---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
const description = 'AI engineering consulting for teams: evaluate use cases, integrate LLMs with tools and data, and build bounded workflows with evaluation and human review.';
const schema = { '@type': 'Service', name: 'AI Engineering Consulting', serviceType: 'AI application engineering and workflow consulting', description, url: `${site.url}/services/ai-engineering/`, provider: { '@id': `${site.url}/#person` } };
---
<Base title="AI Engineering Consulting" description={description} schema={schema}>
  <section class="wrap page-hero"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Services</span></div><div class="eyebrow">01 / AI engineering</div><h1>Make AI useful<br />in the work you actually do.</h1><p class="page-lead">AI engineering consulting for teams that need a clear use case, a working integration, or a path from an impressive prototype to a dependable workflow.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/contact/?topic=ai">Discuss an AI project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><nav class="service-switch" aria-label="Consulting services"><a href="/services/ai-engineering/" aria-current="page">AI engineering</a><a href="/services/devops/">DevOps & cloud ↗</a></nav></section>
  <section class="wrap content-grid"><aside><div class="content-label">WHERE TO START</div><p class="aside-note">A concrete workflow is a better starting point than a model choice.</p></aside><div class="prose"><h2>Turn an open question into a bounded project.</h2><p>You might have an internal process that takes too much manual effort, an AI prototype that works inconsistently, or a team unsure where AI would help. I can help clarify the task, test the important assumptions, and build a useful first version.</p><p>The starting point is the work: what goes in, what needs to come out, how to judge the result, and which decisions require a person.</p><h2>What we can work on</h2><div class="deliverable"><span>01</span><div><h3>Use-case assessment & prototyping</h3><p>Compare a proposed AI workflow with simpler alternatives. Define success, identify data and access requirements, and build a small prototype to test whether the idea deserves further investment.</p></div></div><div class="deliverable"><span>02</span><div><h3>LLM workflows & tool integration</h3><p>Connect models to approved documents, APIs, and internal tools. Design clear task boundaries, handoffs, and review steps for research, document processing, or content operations.</p></div></div><div class="deliverable"><span>03</span><div><h3>Evaluation & operational readiness</h3><p>Build representative examples, inspect failure cases, and establish acceptance checks. Plan for permissions, cost boundaries, observability, and the point where the workflow needs human help.</p></div></div><h2>What a useful handover looks like</h2><p>Depending on the agreed scope, the result could be a documented go/no-go decision, a working integration, or a prototype with an evaluation set and a clear account of its limits. We agree on the deliverable before building.</p><blockquote><p>A useful AI system has a job, a boundary, and a way to know whether it worked.</p></blockquote><h2>Questions you might be asking</h2><div class="faq"><h3>Do we need an agent?</h3><p>Perhaps. A fixed workflow or a conventional integration may be easier to operate. I would first examine what needs to vary and where autonomous decisions add value.</p></div><div class="faq"><h3>Can you work with our existing tools?</h3><p>That is the preferred starting point. We can assess the APIs, data access, permissions, and constraints before deciding what needs to change.</p></div><div class="faq"><h3>Can you help with deployment as well?</h3><p>Yes. AI application work can be scoped together with AWS, Kubernetes, CI/CD, and operational troubleshooting.</p></div><div class="related"><a href="/writing/nemo-guardrails/">Read: NeMo Guardrails: Controlling Chatbot Behavior <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="wrap contact-band"><div><div class="eyebrow">Start with the problem</div><h2>What would useful AI change?</h2><p>Tell me about the workflow, the friction, and the outcome you need.</p></div><a class="button" href="/contact/?topic=ai">Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
</Base>
